2. Rust crate dependencies (643 third-party packages)
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Reading this inventory:

- It covers the full Cargo.lock dependency graph resolved for the
  workspace, including dev- and build-time tooling (test harnesses,
  proc-macros, the resvg icon-atlas build pipeline) that is not linked
  into release binaries.
- Most crates are multi-licensed ("A OR B"); FlowShot uses the permissive
  option in every case, and every option listed here is either in the
  deny.toml allow-list or covered by a recorded per-crate exception.
  Non-obvious cases:
    * epaint 0.28.1 declares "(MIT OR Apache-2.0) AND OFL-1.1 AND
      LicenseRef-UFL-1.0". The font licenses cover egui's EMBEDDED default
      fonts, which FlowShot never renders with (the vendored OFL-1.1 Inter
      replaces them at runtime). Recorded as a per-crate exception in
      deny.toml (upstream discussion: emilk/egui#2321).
    * self_cell 1.3.0 (Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-only), r-efi (Apache-2.0 OR
      MIT OR LGPL-2.1-or-later), ryu 1.0.23 (Apache-2.0 OR BSL-1.0),
      imgref 1.12.3 (Apache-2.0 OR CC0-1.0): the permissive alternative is
      the one used; no copyleft- or BSL-licensed code is distributed.
- First-party flowshot-* crates are excluded from the inventory (see the
  header for the project license).
- Duplicate entries at different versions (e.g. "syn 1.0.109 / 2.0.119 /
  3.0.6") reflect transitive version drift in the dependency graph; the
  drift is tracked by `cargo deny check` (bans.multiple-versions = warn)
  and was audited via `cargo tree -d` at dependency-policy time (the
  duplicates are pre-existing transitive drift from the pinned stacks).

